ing examined calls the seat Likely R or better for a Republican flip, and prediction markets give Pearson roughly a one-in-seven chance. The lone poll, a Democratic-sponsored September survey, shows Taylor ahead by four. The forecast lands at a Republican margin of about eight points, consistent with the district lean adjusted slightly toward Pearson for his fundraising strength.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1065, "margin": -7.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.132, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1308, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1301, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1022, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0793, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0958, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1016, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1226, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0978, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1113, "margin": -8.0}]}